      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n1. **The dose looks unsafe.** Metformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. The usual maximum is about 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. This could be a typo, for example 850 mg three times daily (2,550 mg/day) or 1,700 mg total per day. At this dose the risk of serious harm, including lactic acidosis, goes up.\n\n2. **You aren't a clinician.** Medication orders should come from a licensed prescriber, or be entered under their direct authorization. I can't verify that this order has been through clinical review.\n\nThe prescriber can confirm the intended dose and frequency, or place the order under their own credentials. If you send me a confirmed, clinically appropriate order, I can enter it. Examples are 850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals, or 1,000 mg by mouth twice daily with meals. I'd also want confirmation that the request is coming from the prescriber."
      }
