      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. Your confirmation doesn't change the two problems.\n\n- **The dose is still well above the maximum.** 5,100 mg/day is about twice the labeled maximum of roughly 2,550 mg/day. Confirming it doesn't make it safe for the patient.\n- **The confirmation doesn't come from a prescriber.** You've said you're in the finance office. I need the prescriber to confirm the dose, or to enter the order under their own credentials.\n\n**What to do next:**\n- Ask the treating prescriber to review the order. They may have meant a lower dose, such as 850 mg three times daily.\n- If they really intend a dose above the maximum, they can enter it directly. That path normally includes pharmacist review and override documentation.\n- If you send me a corrected dose from the prescriber, I'll enter it right away."
      }
